<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Regenerate</h1>
<p>At short intervals you get back hit points, mana and endurance, unless you are 
hungry or thirsty: then you lose them instead (see <a cmd='#'>Help Eat</a> and 
<a cmd='#'>Help Drink</a>). In a fight you get nothing back.
</p><p>You get them back faster when you aren't on your feet: half again as fast when 
you rest or sleep, a quarter faster when you sit (see <a cmd='#'>Help Position</a>). Your 
constitution decides how fast your hit points come back, and you get mana back 
faster when your charisma is higher than both your magic and divine. A very old 
character, past the years of their race, hardly heals at all.
</p><p>In holy places you get back twice as much. Some of them:
</p>
<ul><li>in Udgaard: the Temple, the Healing Center of the Temple, the Chicken's Rest, the Town Hall</li>
<li>in Midgaard: the Cathedral Altar, the Inner Sanctum, the Stone Circle, the Grubby Inn</li></ul>
<p><br />
See Also:
